      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their quoted evidence. Tier assignments are appropriate \u2014 PHSO findings and government responses are correctly labelled measurable (they are established facts of record, not projections). The direction 'improves' is justified by the PHSO maladministration finding, which is a concrete institutional basis for an O9 due-process verdict. Magnitude 'moderate' and confidence 'moderate' are reasonable given delivery uncertainty. The rationale is party-blind and does not impute motive. No lever leakage \u2014 the verdict correctly frames the question as whether a formal injustice is remedied, not whether the fiscal cost is worthwhile. No false balance issue \u2014 direction is not mixed/too-uncertain, and the evidence supporting 'improves' (ombudsman finding) is genuine. One minor observation: E12 is backed partly by spectator.com and cityam.com (media/commercial-leaning outlets), but the compensation figure is also corroborated by commonslibrary.parliament.uk context, so this does not rise to blocking. Overall the verdict is publishable."
